Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.59,0:00:09.05,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU, YAMU, YAMU, YAMU, YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.35,0:00:31.47,Default,,0,0,0,,You're on the move!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.19,0:01:06.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Are we there yet? No!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.09,0:01:08.13,Default,,0,0,0,,How about now?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.45,0:01:14.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Behold, the shrine of\Nthe Millennium Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.23,0:01:17.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Follow me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.37,0:01:22.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Dude, this duel is gonna be awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.31,0:01:26.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, Yugi versus the Pharaoh,\Nthat's as good as it gets.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.07,0:01:29.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.59,0:01:31.53,Default,,0,0,0,,What's up, Taya?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.61,0:01:33.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You got to use a little girl's room?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.27,0:01:35.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Not quite.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.18,0:01:38.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I was just wondering why we had\Nto rush into all this so soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.15,0:01:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,This could be our final chance to hang out
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.63,0:01:44.19,Default,,0,0,0,,with the Pharaoh before\Nhe leaves us for good.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.27,0:01:45.10,Default,,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.39,0:01:49.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I was so pumped up for this duel, I\Nforgot this might be his last one.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.87,0:01:50.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, me too.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.11,0:01:58.09,Default,,0,0,0,,My friends, I know how\Ndifficult this must be. However,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.33,0:02:02.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi and the Pharaoh must carry out this\Nbattle ritual as quickly as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.69,0:02:07.21,Default,,0,0,0,,If too much time should pass, our\Nwindow of opportunity will close.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.61,0:02:09.43,Default,,0,0,0,,We all know how you feel, Taya.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.95,0:02:12.21,Default,,0,0,0,,But this is what's best for the Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.29,0:02:17.17,Default,,0,0,0,,He doesn't belong in our world, and now\Nhis spirit finally has a chance to go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.47,0:02:21.30,Default,,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.38,0:02:22.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.51,0:02:25.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I probably don't say this\Nas often as I should, Taya.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.19,0:02:28.85,Default,,0,0,0,,But you know, you're one of\Nthe bravest people I ever met.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.17,0:02:32.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I know this is tough for you,\Nand I just want to say I'm proud.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.55,0:02:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,If you dorks start holding each\Nother's hands, then I'm out of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.25,0:02:39.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't come here to listen to\Nyour lame friendship speeches.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.77,0:02:42.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe if you had some friends,\Nyou wouldn't feel that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.75,0:02:44.27,Default,,0,0,0,,That was harsh, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.93,0:02:46.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh, like you didn't deserve it?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.03,0:02:47.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.07,0:03:02.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That's it!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.25,0:03:05.39,Default,,0,0,0,,The resting place of the\NSeven Millennium Items!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.01,0:03:10.27,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.25,0:03:25.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Before the ritual can begin,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.39,0:03:29.49,Default,,0,0,0,,the Millennium Items must be returned\Nto the stone from whence they came.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.57,0:03:33.01,Default,,0,0,0,,The Eye of Ujjat will then\Npeer into your soul, Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.49,0:03:36.49,Default,,0,0,0,,thus unraveling the Pharaoh's\Nspirit from your own.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.85,0:03:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, if you accept the\Nterms of this ritual,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.73,0:03:45.91,Default,,0,0,0,,then I'll ask you to place the seven\Nitems within the Millennium Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.57,0:04:20.95,Default,,0,0,0,,All of this began the day\NYugi solved that puzzle,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.21,0:04:24.03,Default,,0,0,0,,and it will all end the\Nmoment he returns it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.31,0:04:27.01,Default,,0,0,0,,All right. Here goes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.57,0:04:32.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, puzzle, grant my wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.87,0:04:38.69,Default,,0,0,0,,And my wish did come true.\NThe day I met my friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.97,0:04:52.61,Default,,0,0,0,,And thanks to you, Pharaoh\NI'm ready to give it back
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.91,0:05:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I take it that's supposed\Nto happen, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.37,0:05:14.19,Default,,0,0,0,,The eye is gazing deep within, searching\Nfor the spirit who dwells in Yugi's mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.11,0:05:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Once they are separated,\Nthe ultimate duel can begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.79,0:05:26.05,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the deal?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.03,0:05:31.47,Default,,0,0,0,,The true nature of Yugi's\Nsoul has been revealed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.91,0:05:41.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, I'm seeing double. No,\Nit's the Pharaoh. No way.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.65,0:05:43.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Attempt.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.99,0:05:55.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Go get him, Yugi Uh, you too, Pharaoh
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.65,0:06:00.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, wait So which one of them\Nare we supposed to root for?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.45,0:06:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,If the Pharaoh wins, he gets to stay,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.37,0:06:07.99,Default,,0,0,0,,which means we won't have to say\Ngoodbye We gotta root for Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.07,0:06:11.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Guys, it's the only way to\Nset the Pharaoh's spirit free.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.69,0:06:15.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey's right I should want\Nwhat's best for the Pharaoh
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.87,0:06:19.99,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's for his spirit to\Nmove on I have to be strong
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.85,0:06:25.35,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time. The battle to determine\Ntheir destinies will now begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.27,0:06:35.35,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the first time in my life\Nthat I hope for my opponent's victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.43,0:06:39.37,Default,,0,0,0,,But in order for this duel to truly\Ntest our readiness to separate,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.59,0:06:42.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I must fight with all my strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.05,0:06:45.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Pharaoh,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.11,0:06:50.21,Default,,0,0,0,,now that you've left the Millennium\NPuzzle, I can't hear your thoughts anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.29,0:06:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,But somehow I still know\Nwhat you're thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.29,0:06:54.99,Default,,0,0,0,,And I feel the same way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.91,0:06:57.44,Default,,0,0,0,,If you taught me anything,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.61,0:07:01.83,Default,,0,0,0,,it's to put your heart into your deck\Nand duel with everything you've got.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.91,0:07:04.59,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's exactly what I'm gonna do.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.81,0:07:10.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess we're about to find out\Nwho the true king of games is.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.51,0:07:12.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Here we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.75,0:07:15.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.05,0:07:17.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you ready for this?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.99,0:07:20.46,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what we're here to find out, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.39,0:07:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's duel!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.03,0:07:28.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Best of luck, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.87,0:07:30.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Now,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.78,0:07:33.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll start by discarding\None card from my hand
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.59,0:07:36.51,Default,,0,0,0,,in order to summon a\Nmonster known as the Tricky.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.71,0:07:42.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I place one card\Nface down and end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.19,0:07:47.35,Default,,0,0,0,,His monster may have 2,000\Npoints, but I know how to stop it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.85,0:07:49.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Check this out!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.53,0:07:53.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate my Swords of Revealing Light!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.81,0:07:59.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that monster can't\Nattack for three more turns.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.21,0:08:03.57,Default,,0,0,0,,and next i'll call my green\Ngadget to the field in
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.65,0:08:08.89,Default,,0,0,0,,attack mode and thanks to his\Nspecial power i can move red
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.97,0:08:13.89,Default,,0,0,0,,gadget to my hand then i\Nplace one card face down and
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.97,0:08:18.59,Default,,0,0,0,,that's all for now you think\Nthat's good watch this i may not
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.67,0:08:21.93,Default,,0,0,0,,be able to attack yuki with\Nmy monster but i can attack
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.01,0:08:27.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Him with his own. I activate\Nthe magic card Rebellion now!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.03,0:08:31.07,Default,,0,0,0,,i can select a monster on your\Nside of the field and force
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.15,0:08:35.53,Default,,0,0,0,,it to attack you directly and\Ni choose your green gadget
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.99,0:08:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,hold on you triggered my trap so now i
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.99,0:08:49.87,Default,,0,0,0,,activate stronghold the moving fortress
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.39,0:09:01.97,Default,,0,0,0,,This trap is also a monster with 2,000\Ndefense points, so my life points are safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.01,0:09:09.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid your life points\Naren't as safe as you think, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.37,0:09:13.23,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.71,0:09:15.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Green Gadget was Yugi's monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.39,0:09:20.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't say I've ever seen a duel\Nas evenly matched as this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.31,0:09:21.43,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you expect?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.55,0:09:23.67,Default,,0,0,0,,These guys shared a brain for years.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.35,0:09:27.94,Default,,0,0,0,,We never had those cards\Nin our deck before.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.25,0:09:31.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I wonder what other\Nsurprises Yugi has in store.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.67,0:09:35.93,Default,,0,0,0,,With this new deck I've assembled,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.25,0:09:39.31,Default,,0,0,0,,the Pharaoh's never going\Nto figure out my strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.33,0:09:42.33,Default,,0,0,0,,His cards may keep me guessing,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.61,0:09:44.79,Default,,0,0,0,,but do they have what\Nit takes to stand up to
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.87,0:09:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,the most powerful\Ncreatures in Duel Monsters?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.59,0:09:49.47,Default,,0,0,0,,The Egyptian Gods?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.45,0:09:56.73,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Pharaoh, my move!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.53,0:10:01.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate Ties of the Brethren!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.43,0:10:05.03,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I pay a thousand life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.47,0:10:09.45,Default,,0,0,0,,After that, I'm able to summon two\Nlevel four monsters from my deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.53,0:10:12.65,Default,,0,0,0,,And I know just what I need. Come forth!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.97,0:10:15.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Red Gadget and Yellow Gadget!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.69,0:10:17.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Take the field into Fence Mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.39,0:10:24.35,Default,,0,0,0,,It will take more than a strong\Ndefense to win this duel, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.71,0:10:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not done yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.31,0:10:28.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, gadgets!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.99,0:10:30.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Join my stronghold!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.17,0:10:48.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever these three gadget monsters\Nare on the field at the same time,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.31,0:10:53.45,Default,,0,0,0,,They're able to raise the attack strength\Nof my Moving Fortress to 3,000 points!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.87,0:10:56.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I taught that kid\Neverything he knows, folks.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.05,0:11:00.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Stronghold, the Moving Fortress, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.11,0:11:02.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Steel Gear Crush!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.29,0:11:09.27,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened to my Stronghold?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.73,0:11:13.39,Default,,0,0,0,,He's trapped thanks to my Bounce spell.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.71,0:11:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,This magic card allowed me to transfer the
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.07,0:11:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,effect of your Swords of\NRevealing Light to your
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.95,0:11:22.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Monster now it can't attack\Nfor three more turns.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.47,0:11:26.57,Default,,0,0,0,,now what am i gonna do\Ni wasn't expecting that
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.65,0:11:29.05,Default,,0,0,0,,i guess the pharaoh really\Nis trying his hardest
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.13,0:11:34.17,Default,,0,0,0,,to defeat me i switch my green gadget into
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.25,0:11:38.13,Default,,0,0,0,,defense mode and end my\Nturn you in my heart i
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.21,0:11:40.99,Default,,0,0,0,,hope you win but that\Ndoesn't mean i plan to go
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.79,0:11:43.62,Default,,0,0,0,,easy on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.70,0:11:44.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my move.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.01,0:11:48.09,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'll start by sending\Nmy monster to the graveyard
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.17,0:11:51.77,Default,,0,0,0,,in order to activate the\Nmagic card Tricky Spell 4.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.17,0:11:56.94,Default,,0,0,0,,This allows me to summon as many tricky\Ntokens as you have monsters on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.41,0:12:00.13,Default,,0,0,0,,That gives me four monsters as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.41,0:12:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa, the taller Yugi\Njust evened it all up.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.19,0:12:04.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Not exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.37,0:12:08.61,Default,,0,0,0,,If he's about to do what I think he\Nis, then he's way ahead of the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.99,0:12:12.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not finished yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.79,0:12:13.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Not even close.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.33,0:12:17.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm taking this duel to\Nthe next level. No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.69,0:12:18.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.79,0:12:24.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I sacrifice three of my tokens,\Nso I can play Obelisk the Tormentor!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.03,0:12:33.65,Default,,0,0,0,,No! Now what?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.11,0:12:43.21,Default,,0,0,0,,This could present a problem.\NWell, maybe for your average.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.29,0:12:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,dooms but we're talking about\Nyuki here remember i know
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.99,0:12:50.15,Default,,0,0,0,,yuki's good but he's up\Nagainst an egyptian god here
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.23,0:12:55.35,Default,,0,0,0,,obelisk attack destroy his\Nfortress with your fist of fate
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.67,0:13:10.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I place one card face down\Nand that ends my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.29,0:13:14.25,Default,,0,0,0,,yuki you gotta hang in\Nthere dude the pharaoh meets
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.33,0:13:18.91,Default,,0,0,0,,business no joke poor guy\Nnot only did he get clobbered
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.99,0:13:21.63,Default,,0,0,0,,by obelisk but thanks to\Nswords of Revealing light,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.71,0:13:22.95,Default,,0,0,0,,he can't strike back.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.05,0:13:26.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you I wouldn't go easy on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.27,0:13:32.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Check it out, guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.85,0:13:35.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's back on his feet. Big deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.63,0:13:38.47,Default,,0,0,0,,There's still no way he\Ncan stand up to Obelisk.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.91,0:13:40.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Then why is he smiling?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.73,0:13:44.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps Yugi wants to lose so\Nthe pharaoh doesn't have to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.73,0:13:46.07,Default,,0,0,0,,No way, Bakura.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.37,0:13:50.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi may not want to say goodbye, but\Nthere's no way he'd be happy about losing.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.83,0:13:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,So why the smile?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.49,0:13:54.43,Default,,0,0,0,,He's having the time of his life.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.93,0:13:56.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Think about it, Taya.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.19,0:13:58.84,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Yugi's shot to\Nfinally prove himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.43,0:14:02.31,Default,,0,0,0,,He usually takes a back seat during duels.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.49,0:14:05.37,Default,,0,0,0,,But this time, Yugi's in\Ncontrol of his own deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.05,0:14:08.82,Default,,0,0,0,,So now, instead of standing\Nbehind the Pharaoh,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.05,0:14:12.58,Default,,0,0,0,,the two of them are standing\Nface-to-face for one last duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.13,0:14:14.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but can Yugi win?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.89,0:14:16.07,Default,,0,0,0,,It's gonna be tough.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.21,0:14:18.29,Default,,0,0,0,,But if anyone can do it, Yugi can.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.69,0:14:20.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take things from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.83,0:14:23.54,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I'll place these\Nthree cards face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.43,0:14:27.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And then I summon my Silent\NSwordsman to the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.45,0:14:31.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's how he kicked Bacora's butt.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.87,0:14:33.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, the evil one.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.85,0:14:36.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Now let's see if you can get past him.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.51,0:14:38.63,Default,,0,0,0,,What's he thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.29,0:14:43.03,Default,,0,0,0,,One attack by Obelisk the\NTormentor and Yugi loses the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.31,0:14:44.99,Default,,0,0,0,,That geek's up to something.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.51,0:14:47.67,Default,,0,0,0,,This could just be my last move.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.13,0:14:50.49,Default,,0,0,0,,To begin, I'll place one card face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.05,0:14:54.49,Default,,0,0,0,,And next, I'll play my card\Nof Sanctity. Magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.33,0:14:59.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Now we both draw until we're each\Nholding six cards in our hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.53,0:15:02.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.89,0:15:04.65,Default,,0,0,0,,As ready as I'll ever be.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.21,0:15:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, here goes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.93,0:15:09.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid if this\Nworks, the duel is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.19,0:15:13.85,Default,,0,0,0,,May the heart of the cards\Nguide you, Yugi. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.37,0:15:18.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Now let's see if you can withstand\Nthe great fury of an Egyptian god.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.89,0:15:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Go ahead!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.99,0:15:21.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me your best shot, Pharaoh!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.13,0:15:25.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Obelisk the Tormentor, attack\Nhis Silent Swordsman now!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.55,0:15:30.67,Default,,0,0,0,,End this duel with your Fist of Fate!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.21,0:15:37.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Look out!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.79,0:15:39.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I reveal my trap!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.91,0:15:41.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Ground Erosion!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.53,0:15:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, I activate a magic\Ncard known as Turn Jump!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.27,0:15:48.53,Default,,0,0,0,,It forces each player to\Njump ahead three turns,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.75,0:15:51.87,Default,,0,0,0,,during which neither of us\Nis allowed to make a move!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.51,0:15:58.23,Default,,0,0,0,,This lets my swordsman increase\Nfrom level zero to level three!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.37,0:16:04.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Well done, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.19,0:16:07.54,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's not enough to defeat Obelisk!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.41,0:16:09.24,Default,,0,0,0,,You're wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.43,0:16:12.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to the effect of my\Nground erosion trap card,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.11,0:16:15.17,Default,,0,0,0,,your Egyptian god is weaker\Nthan you think, Pharaoh!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.27,0:16:17.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Traps don't work on Obelisk.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.63,0:16:19.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not using it on him.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.41,0:16:22.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm using it on the\Nfield under him. But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.81,0:16:23.64,Default,,0,0,0,,It's simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.93,0:16:25.57,Default,,0,0,0,,After ground erosion is played,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.65,0:16:27.61,Default,,0,0,0,,the monster standing on\Nmy opponent's side of
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.69,0:16:31.01,Default,,0,0,0,,the field loses 500 points\Nwith each passing turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.95,0:16:35.75,Default,,0,0,0,,And thanks to my magic card,\Nthree turns have just gone by.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.97,0:16:41.99,Default,,0,0,0,,So Obelisk loses 1,500 attack points,\Nmaking its strength equal to my swordsman's.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.07,0:16:46.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Big deal, Yugi. So now the\Nduel's at a standstill. Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.95,0:16:52.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Not so fast I activated a\Ntrap card of my own Behold,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.97,0:16:54.27,Default,,0,0,0,,my summoning clock
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.25,0:16:57.93,Default,,0,0,0,,It's automatically triggered\Nwhenever you play a
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.01,0:17:01.73,Default,,0,0,0,,magic or trap card Now all\NI have to do is sacrifice
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.81,0:17:05.51,Default,,0,0,0,,my clock and one monster\Nfrom the field Then I can
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.59,0:17:09.11,Default,,0,0,0,,summon one new beast for\Neach turn that's passed What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.51,0:17:10.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Three new monsters?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.39,0:17:12.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.87,0:17:15.87,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'll start with Queen's\NKnight and King's Knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.95,0:17:18.83,Default,,0,0,0,,which lets me automatically\Nsummon Jack's Knight!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.43,0:17:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,One left.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.99,0:17:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,So I summon Slifer the Sky Dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.51,0:17:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.87,0:17:27.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Another Egyptian god?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.41,0:17:51.37,Default,,0,0,0,,As you know, Slifer receives a thousand\Nattack points for every card in my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.65,0:17:53.63,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm holding three cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.41,0:17:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You just triggered my trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.61,0:18:02.13,Default,,0,0,0,,It's called Ambush Shield, and I'll\Nactivate it by sacrificing this card.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.37,0:18:03.73,Default,,0,0,0,,My red gadget.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.07,0:18:08.37,Default,,0,0,0,,So now I get to add its defense\Npoints to my soldier's attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.49,0:18:10.31,Default,,0,0,0,,That is one powerful knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.39,0:18:14.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It even has enough points to\Ndefeat Slifer the Sky Dragon now.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.09,0:18:15.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Very impressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.43,0:18:18.67,Default,,0,0,0,,However, your two gadget\Nmonsters are still vulnerable.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.05,0:18:20.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, my knights, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.71,0:18:30.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Luckily for you, my\Nturn's just about done.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.95,0:18:34.79,Default,,0,0,0,,All I need to do now is call\None final monster to the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.93,0:18:41.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I sacrifice my queen's knight, my\Njack's knight, and my king's knight!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.49,0:18:44.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Is he? He is!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.33,0:18:50.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Almighty protector of the solid sky,\NI beg of thee, please heed my cry.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.01,0:18:53.25,Default,,0,0,0,,The ancient chant, he knows it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.35,0:18:58.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Transform thyself from orb of light,\Nand bring me victory in this fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.57,0:19:04.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I beseech thee, grace our humble game,\Nbut first I shall call out thy name!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.79,0:19:06.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Winged Dragon of Ra!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.49,0:19:13.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Behold the third Egyptian god!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.79,0:19:19.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Now what's Yugi gonna do?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.23,0:19:37.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Unbelievable, he played all three Egyptian
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.27,0:19:42.57,Default,,0,0,0,,gods at once yugi the\Ntrue test will now begin
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.59,0:19:58.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, oh, oh,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.81,0:20:02.69,Default,,0,0,0,,oh.
